\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Architecture of the Gaussian diffusion flows \cite  {sohl2015diffusion,ho2020ddpm}. Forward steps (blue) use the noise schedule and Gaussian innovations. Backward steps (orange) start from fresh noise; a neural model predicts reverse-distribution parameters and a Gaussian sampler produces the next state. The displayed neural outputs follow the 2015 formulation; DDPM's noise-based mean parameterization is introduced in Section~\ref {sec:parameterization}. The learned intermediate steps are shown; the final-step boundary is discussed in the text.}}{4}{figure.caption.1}\protected@file@percent }
